---
import { faMapMarkerAlt } from "@fortawesome/free-solid-svg-icons";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import GetInTouchButton from "./GetInTouchButton.astro";
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
import headshot from "../images/Headshot.png";
import { getHoursSpentBuildingSoftware, getYearsCoding } from "../utils/experience";

const fastFacts = [
  `${getYearsCoding()}+ years coding experience`,
  `${getHoursSpentBuildingSoftware()}+ hours spent building software`,
  "2+ years writing pedagogy experience",
];
---

<div class="row introduction-row">
  <div class="col-10 offset-1 col-3k-8 offset-3k-2 col-4k-6 offset-4k-3">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-8 col-2k-7 col-3k-6 col-4k-5">
        <div class="row align-items-center">
          <div class="col-8 offset-2 col-sm-4 offset-sm-0 col-md-3 col-lg-4 col-xl-3">
            <Image
              src={headshot}
              alt="A photo of me"
              width={200}
              height={200}
              densities={[1, 2]}
              loading="eager"
              fetchpriority="high"
              class="headshot"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="col-12 col-sm-8 col-md-9 col-lg-8 col-xl-9">
            <h1 class="name text-center text-sm-start">Jeff Terry</h1>
            {/* Only show on larger screens */}
            <p class="job-title d-none d-sm-block">
              <span class="me-3">Software Engineer in</span>
              <span class="nowrap">
                <Icon icon={faMapMarkerAlt} class="me-2" />
                <span>Chapel Hill, NC</span>
              </span>
            </p>
          </div>

          {/* Hide on larger screens */}
          <div class="col-12 d-sm-none text-center">
            <p class="job-title">
              <span class="me-2 me-sm-3">Software Engineer in</span>
              <span class="nowrap">
                <Icon icon={faMapMarkerAlt} class="me-2" />
                <span>Chapel Hill, NC</span>
              </span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row fast-facts-row">
          {
            fastFacts.map((fact) => (
              <div class="col-12 col-sm-11 offset-sm-1 text-center text-sm-start fast-fact-col">
                <p class="fast-fact">{fact}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>

        {/* Show only on large screens */}
        <div class="row d-none d-lg-flex">
          <div class="col-12 text-center mt-5">
            <GetInTouchButton />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-4 col-2k-5 col-3k-6 col-4k-7 biography-col" data-biography>
        <p>
          Hi, I’m Jeff, a software engineer based in North Carolina. My professional background is
          primarily in full-stack software engineering, but I’ve done work in a variety of
          areas—from robotics, to infrastructure / DevOps, to data engineering. I’m obsessed with
          building software that improves people’s lives, and I’m always excited to learn whatever
          languages and technologies I need to make that happen!
        </p>
        <p>
          I’m currently at <a href="https://spade.com">Spade</a> (YC W22), where we're building the
          data and AI platform for modern finance. As Spade's first engineering hire, I helped
          spearhead the buildout of our transaction enrichment API—including infrastructure,
          backend, developer tooling, CI/CD pipelines, testing strategy, monitoring and logging
          systems, etc...—while helping to establish our engineering team culture and processes.
        </p>
        <div id="biography-more" hidden>
          <p>
            At Spade, the systems I've built and the projects I've led have enabled us to maintain
            an historical uptime above 99.999% and to achieve latencies more than 10x lower than
            those of competitors (in an uptime- and latency-critical space!).
          </p>
          <p>
            Recently, I've been focusing my efforts on improving Spade's data pipelines. For
            instance, I've led projects to increase our underlying data quality, to improve the
            stability of our pipelines, and to create tooling to empower the data science team to
            move more quickly and collaborate more easily. As an example, one project I led ended up
            achieving a 50% increase in the accuracy of our lat/lon data (which was more than even I
            thought we could achieve, and I tend to be a pretty optimistic person)!
          </p>
          <p>
            Previously, I was a full-stack engineer at Concertiv, where I led the development of
            their B2B product procurement platform, integrating workflow tools, contract management,
            and spend analysis to help companies optimize B2B spend. Before that, I worked as a
            software engineering intern for Microsoft, National Instruments, and a few other
            companies, in addition to co-founding a company back in college.
          </p>
          <p>
            Outside of tech, I’ve worked as a writing tutor and a rhetoric instructor at the
            university level. As part of my graduate studies at The Ohio State University, I focused
            on two research areas: 1) The impacts of technology on society and the human experience
            during the Modernist era (~1880–1918; an era that closely mirrors our own, in fact!) and
            2) Digital media studies and software usability. My work in the latter area culminated
            in <a href="https://presly.org">Presly</a>, an online presentation coach that teaches
            students how to give great presentations.
          </p>
          <p>
            My passion for software (and building things more generally) began in the field of
            robotics, when two friends and I won an international high school robotics competition
            as eighth graders, a competition we went on to win two more times once we became proper
            high schoolers. Here's a <a href="https://goo.gl/vQMIP2"
              >video of two of my favorite robots</a
            >. My experience working in robotics encouraged a first-principles-based, goal-oriented,
            and honest approach to engineering, which still drives my work today.
          </p>
        </div>
        <button class="read-more-button" aria-controls="biography-more" aria-expanded="false">
          Read more
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Hide on large screens */}
    <div class="row d-lg-none">
      <div class="col-12 text-center mt-5">
        <GetInTouchButton />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  // Clicking anywhere in the biography (other than a link) expands or collapses it
  const biography = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-biography]")!;
  const more = biography.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#biography-more")!;
  const button = biography.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(".read-more-button")!;

  biography.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    if ((event.target as Element).closest("a")) return;
    const expanded = more.hidden;
    more.hidden = !expanded;
    button.textContent = expanded ? "Read less" : "Read more";
    button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(expanded));
  });
</script>

<style>
  .introduction-row {
    padding-bottom: 70px;
  }

  .headshot {
    display: block;
  }

  .name {
    font-size: 3.25rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 576px) {
    .name {
      font-size: 4rem;
      margin-top: 0;
      text-align: left;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .name {
      font-size: 5rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 992px) {
    .name {
      font-size: 4rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1200px) {
    .name {
      font-size: 5rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1600px) {
    .name {
      font-size: 6rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1800px) {
    .name {
      font-size: 7rem;
    }
  }

  .job-title {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 576px) {
    .job-title {
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1600px) {
    .job-title {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1800px) {
    .job-title {
      font-size: 1.85rem;
    }
  }

  .fast-facts-row {
    margin-top: 25px;
  }

  .fast-fact-col {
    margin-top: 15px;
  }

  .fast-fact {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 576px) {
    .fast-fact {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1600px) {
    .fast-fact {
      font-size: 1.9rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1800px) {
    .fast-fact {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }

  .biography-col {
    cursor: default;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .biography-col p {
    text-align: left;
  }
  @media (min-width: 992px) {
    .biography-col {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1600px) {
    .biography-col {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1800px) {
    .biography-col {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 2000px) {
    .biography-col {
      font-size: 1.375rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 2200px) {
    .biography-col {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 2800px) {
    .biography-col {
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 3400px) {
    .biography-col {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 3800px) {
    .biography-col {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }

  .read-more-button {
    color: inherit;
    background-color: unset;
    border: unset;
    padding: unset;
    display: inline;
    text-align: center;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
